            <title>[LU-21099] alloc_workqueue() WARNs on Linux 7.2: neither WQ_PERCPU nor WQ_UNBOUND</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21099</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Linux 7.2 includes commit 21c05ca88a54 ("workqueue: Add warnings and ensure one among WQ_PERCPU or WQ_UNBOUND is present"). alloc_workqueue() now WARNs, with a full stack trace, when it is given neither flag, and then sets WQ_PERCPU itself. WQ_PERCPU was added in 930c2ea566af (v6.17).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Seen on every module load on Amazon Linux 2027, kernel 7.2.8 (x86_64 and aarch64), with the 2.15 client:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;workqueue: cfs_rh is using neither WQ_PERCPU or WQ_UNBOUND. Setting WQ_PERCPU.
WARNING: kernel/workqueue.c:5851 at __alloc_workqueue+0x468/0x4d0
 ... libcfs_init+0xab/0x2b0 [libcfs]
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Behaviour is unchanged, since per-CPU was already the default, but the WARN panics hosts running with panic_on_warn.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;On master these alloc_workqueue() callers pass neither flag:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul class="alternate" type="square"&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre/obdclass/hash.c: cfs_rh&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lnet/klnds/kfilnd/kfilnd.c: kfilnd_wq&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre/ptlrpc/gss/gss_svc_upcall.c: gss_cleanup_wq&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;lustre/osd-ldiskfs/osd_handler.c: %s-integrityd&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;p&gt;Fix: pass WQ_PERCPU explicitly, with a configure check that defines WQ_PERCPU as 0 on kernels that lack it.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
